1
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:06,000
See it early. Avoid the mob.

2
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:06,000
Jane Austen's Mafia! is a comedy, crime film directed by Jim Abrahams.

3
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:06,000
After growing up poor in Salmonella, Vincenzo Cortino installs himself as
the preeminent, if bumbling, Mafia don of the New World.

4
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:06,000
But now he must pass on power to one of his two sons: either
level-headed veteran Anthony or vituperative loose cannon Joey.

5
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:06,000
Anthony Cortino, played by Jay Mohr.

6
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:06,000
Joey Cortino, played by Billy Burke.

7
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:06,000
Diane Steen, played by Christina Applegate.

8
00:32:00,000 --> 00:32:06,000
Pepper Gianini, played by Pamela Gidley.

9
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
Sophia, played by Olympia Dukakis.

10
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:06,000
Vincenzo Cortino, played by Lloyd Bridges.

11
00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:06,000
Mafia!, also known as Jane Austen's Mafia!, is a 1998 American crime parody film directed by Jim Abrahams and
starring Jay Mohr, Lloyd Bridges (in one of his final films), Olympia Dukakis and Christina Applegate.

12
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
It was Abrahams’ final directorial effort before his death in 2024.

13
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:06,000
The film spoofs Francis Ford Coppola's Godfather series and various
other mafia films, notably Martin Scorsese's Casino (1995).

14
00:56:00,000 --> 00:56:06,000
It also parodies films in other genres, ranging from Forrest
Gump to Il Postino and The English Patient.

15
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
In the film, a Korean War veteran avenges an
assassination attempt on his crime boss father.

16
01:04:00,000 --> 01:04:06,000
The veteran subsequently manages a casino in Las Vegas,
until surviving another assassination attempt.

17
01:08:00,000 --> 01:08:06,000
He sets out to gain vengeance, and to regain the love of his ex-girlfriend.

18
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
By that point his girlfriend had been elected as the President of the United States,
and he has to convince her to postpone her plans for world peace.

19
01:16:00,000 --> 01:16:06,000
The film explores themes of escape, italy, sicily, italy, gangster, postman.

20
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
The tone is lighthearted.
